APPENDIX A. INSTALLATION ACCEPTANCE TEXT

 The following is recommended click-through wording and implementation guidance for a license-acceptance interface. Both acknowledgements must be separate and unchecked by default. 

A.1. First required acknowledgement — informed review of risks:

☐ I confirm that I have reviewed UTU Engine EULA and the risk notices for diagnostic tools and external integrations I intend to enable. I understand that diagnostic queries may degrade connected services; LLM outputs require independent human verification; source-data masking can fail; and when an external AI endpoint or messaging channel is configured and used, incident and diagnostic information, potentially including sensitive data, may be transmitted to the selected third-party provider or recipients. 

A.2. Second required acknowledgement — contractual acceptance:

☐ I have read and accept the UTU Engine End User License Agreement, including the restrictions on resale, bundling and commercialization. If I accept on behalf of an organization, I confirm that I am authorized to bind that organization. 

A.3. Implementation requirements: display the complete EULA or provide an immediately accessible copy; separately link tool-specific risk documentation; show both checkboxes unchecked; block the acceptance action until both are affirmatively selected; retain a reliable record identifying the exact accepted text and date/time. 

A.4. If a person accepts for an organization, present a clear statement that the person confirms authority to bind that organization. No UI design should imply that the first risk acknowledgement alone constitutes acceptance of the EULA. 

A.5. Where the Software supports an external AI provider or third-party notification service, the installation or configuration workflow should separately disclose the selected destination, categories of information normally sent, and relevant outbound-data risks before the integration is enabled. This operational notice does not replace any personal-data notice, contract or consent required by law. 

A.6. Any consent or acknowledgement should be recorded with the exact accepted text or its cryptographic digest, timestamp and accepting authority where lawful; if material terms change, the applicable legal requirements for renewed acceptance should be assessed. Consent to this EULA must not be represented as consent given by third-party data subjects.


